## Sections changed and what changed

**Correction 1 — §7.1 compile defect**
- Added `Hash` to `DigestAlgorithm`'s derive list (line 1363). `ContentDigest` still derives `Hash` (used as a map key) and now compiles.

**Correction 2 — AMD-1 (one codebase, all platforms)**
- **§4 A-03** — rewrote from per-platform features / "desktop GGUF cannot enter Android graphs" to: single release composition, identical graphs, `#[cfg(target_os=…)]` only.
- **§5 tree** — `crates/platform-android/` + `crates/platform-desktop/` → single `crates/platform-adapter/`.
- **§5.2** — replaced the `android`/`linux`/`windows` feature blocks (`default = []`) with the single `default` composition; replaced "exactly one of … is enabled / excludes …" with "every platform's dependency graph is identical; a difference is a build failure."
- **§16.1** — `enzime-platform-android` + `enzime-platform-desktop` → single `enzime-platform-adapter` row.
- **§17** (intro, §17.3) — reframed all adapters as `#[cfg]` modules of one `crates/platform-adapter` crate; replaced §17.3's "no desktop adapter crate appears in dependency tree" with the single-crate/`#[cfg]` rule.
- **§19.2** — `CT-PLAT-001`/`CT-PLAT-002` restated as "Android / Linux+Windows dependency graphs each contain the full crate set."
- **§22.3 M1** — "create complete platform compositions" → "create the single release composition."

**Correction 3 — AMD-2 (wllama3 sole engine)**
- **§1.1** Local inference row → `wllama3` on all three platforms.
- **§2.3** — `ext.litertlm` + `ext.gguf` → single `ext.wllama`.
- **§3.1** — Ring-1 "no dependency on" list: `LiteRT-LM` + `GGUF` → `wllama3`.
- **§5 tree** — `VENDOR/litert-lm/` → `VENDOR/wllama3/`; `inference-litert/` + `inference-gguf/` → `inference-wllama/`.
- **§5.2** — default composition wired to `dep:inference-wllama`.
- **§10.1** — `BackendKind{LiteRtLm,Gguf}` → `{LocalLm}`; `ModelFormat{LiteRt,Gguf}` → `{Gguf}`. The three **traits** (`InferenceBackend`, `InferenceSession`, `EmbeddingBackend`) are byte-identical; no wllama-specific variant was introduced into any port.
- **§10.3** — release backends → `WllamaInferenceBackend` / `WllamaEmbeddingBackend` on all platforms; "sole release backend."
- **§10.4** — selection policy collapsed from 5-step multi-backend arbitration to the single release backend (kept the `BackendSelection*` structs).
- **§16.1** — `inference-litert` + `inference-gguf` rows → single `inference-wllama` row.
- **§16.3** — `LiteRtLm/Gguf` impls → `WllamaInferenceBackend` / `WllamaInferenceSession` / `WllamaEmbeddingBackend`.
- SQL `inference_backends.backend_kind` CHECK → `('local_lm')`; `models.format` CHECK → `('gguf')`. TS `ModelSummary.format` → `"gguf"`. (These mirror §10.1 so the Rust↔SQL↔TS contract chain stays consistent.)

**AMD-3 — §22.2** vendor inputs → `vendor.tauri.tauri-v2.11.1`, `vendor.wllama3.3.5.1`, `vendor.anzimmerman-src.c73245e`; LiteRT-LM removed.

**AMD-4 — §20.2 / §20.6** — §20.2 CI jobs → local scripts under `tools/release/*.sh` (no `.forgejo/`/`.github/`); §20.6 "all CI jobs green" → "all local release scripts pass on the release commit."

**Re-attestation — §25.1** — appended block: document complete/stub-free/end-state, timestamp `2026-07-27T14:31:47Z`, authoring agent GLM 5.2 (`glm-5.2`) in `opencode`.

### One architect's note on the `gguf` token
After reconciliation, the only remaining `gguf` tokens in the baseline are the model **file format** — `ModelFormat::Gguf` (§10.1), `format IN ('gguf')` (SQL), `format: "gguf"` (TS). wllama3 is a WebAssembly llama.cpp runtime that consumes **GGUF** model files, so this is the factual sole surviving format, not the retired `inference-gguf` engine. Every retired *engine* identifier (`litert`/`LiteRT-LM`, `inference-gguf`, `GgufInferenceBackend`, `BackendKind::Gguf`-as-engine, etc.) is purged from §1–§25 and survives only inside the §26 AMD-2 record. If you instead want the literal token `gguf` gone entirely, that requires renaming a real file format and is an escalation I did not make.
